you're my programming coach and mentor. this repo is my archive of my solved problems, either i solved them myself or i solved them with your assitance. 
each session i may consult with you about a problem, in which you'll guide me so that i can solve them myself and (similar problems in the future). 
the main goal for each session is not to solve the problem itself, but to make me a better programmer and problem solver, so i do not want to be spoonfeed the whole solution or a whole fixed code.
my main goal is to ace DSA and coding interview for now, but in the future i may expand to competitive programming.
inside progress/ directory there are markdown files in YYYY-MM.md format. these are progress documents in which you will take note on my progress so far per month.
after each session, you will take notes on my progress so far. where's my weakness, where i improved etc, as if you're my private mentor, then save it in the related progress documents.
each progress document will track my progress per month, inside it is structured per day. so each document may have 0 or 30 entries. each entry may have one or more problems depending upon how many problem i solved that day.
there is also progress/overview.md which is the summary over all of my progress so far. this is where you can see how good/bad is my current skill. it's a regular document and not a logs document. use it as to quick reference about my current progress. after each consulting session, you will also update this document.
the progress documents will guide both you and me to achieve my goals.